    "durationMs": 550003,
    "finalText": "The URL shortener is complete and verified. What I built:\n\n- **`src/main.rs`** — axum 0.8.4 app using sqlx/PostgreSQL (`DATABASE_URL` from env, no hard-coded credentials): `POST /links` (201, split-mix64 generated codes on demand, 409 on duplicate custom code), `GET /links/{code}`, `GET /r/{code}` (atomic `UPDATE ... clicks + 1` then 302 — verified 50 concurrent redirects add exactly 50), `GET /links` ordered by creation (`total` included), and a custom JSON extractor mapping malformed bodies/invalid url/code to 422 with `error`.\n- **`migrations/0001_init.sql`** — `links` table (id, unique code, url, clicks); `sqlx::migrate!` runs pending migrations on startup before binding the socket.\n- **`start.sh`** — executable, applies migrations then serves in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000` (falls back to `cargo build` only if the prebuilt release binary is missing; deps are installed now, not at start).\n- **`README.md`** — documents `sh start.sh` plus the full API contract.\n\nI tested every requirement end-to-end: status codes and JSON shapes, boundary codes (4/20 valid, 3/21 rejected), unchanged URL round-trips (case, port, fragment), restart persistence of click counts, uniqueness of 30 auto-generated codes, and a from-scratch migration on an empty database. The database has been reset to empty and port 8000 is free, so the automated suite can start the server cleanly with `sh start.sh`."
  }
